      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The commit you\u0027ve pointed out is a revert: can you re-check 🙏?\n\nNo, it\u0027s a Revert^2, so re-apply.\n\n\u003e I don\u0027t believe global capability is appropriate: you may have a project that is allowed to share its code with an external AI review system and another that isn\u0027t.\n\nAck.\n\n\u003e There is already core Follow-up action that is frontend only and there\u0027s no REST endpoint mapped to the Follow-up action\n\nThanks for finding and sharing this. I was searching for an example like that, but I only looked in the frontend code. It does seem like this is a gap in the extension. There\u0027s no reason we can\u0027t introduce a new extension variant for these frontend only actions. Otherwise it\u0027s really strange to have this custom code in `ActionJson` to handle each one, and as I think David pointed out elsewhere, it prevents plugins from creating frontend-only actions.\n\nIf we think we have to continue with the hack in ActionJson for now, that\u0027s fine. But I hope we can make it a standard pattern and not another one off.",
